  "limits": [
    "Bounded new native qualification covers the documented Mode2 configuration and supplied external test projects, not arbitrary scenes, NTSC or physical hardware.",
    "Legacy/default, old rotation and Q8 preserve their renderer contracts. Compatibility corrected/camera/rotation profiles are documented separately; prior numerical/native reports are not relabelled as new universal qualification.",
    "Positions must stay inside the relative Q4 camera domain; inspect legacy_camera_fault. Signed screen-span limits and assembly IO guards remain enabled.",
    "Wide projected offsets use the inherited integer screen fallback. The new near/screen Q4 pass requires ordinary near-poly, camera-plane profile0 and world-ground-plane clip0.",
    "The4096-phase public camera API consumes fractional input. Legacy keyboard controls do not automatically gain fractional angular steps.",
    "Frozen poses prove geometry and deterministic buffers, not FPS. Finite Q4 precision and integer raster are not pixel-exact float or Q8 guarantees.",
    "All raw commands, captures, scenes, motions and measured PRGs stay in the separate qualification folder; none are shipped in the source SDK."
